From 231efbcc6e993f0d0996ce050faae15ab0cecccd Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Lance <Gero3977@gmail.com>
Date: Sun, 2 Aug 2026 03:52:53 -0700
Subject: [PATCH 4/6] drm/msm/adreno: keep A540 active across runtime PM

The LG V30 A540 wedges the MSM8998 GPU interconnect after the first runtime power collapse. K126/K127 isolated this from firmware loading and command submission: holding one runtime-PM reference kept repeated GL submits stable, while releasing it made the next resume stall before the first A5xx resume register write.

Replace the bring-up-only module parameter with a device-managed reference for A540. The reference is acquired only after successful hardware initialization, is balanced automatically at driver teardown, and does not bypass the force-suspend callbacks used for system sleep.

This is a bounded stability workaround, not a claim that the underlying A540 collapse sequence is fixed.

Assisted-by: Aurel/Hermes:openai-codex:gpt-5.6-sol
Signed-off-by: Lance <Gero3977@gmail.com>
---
 drivers/gpu/drm/msm/adreno/adreno_device.c | 11 +++++++++++
 1 file changed, 11 insertions(+)

diff --git a/drivers/gpu/drm/msm/adreno/adreno_device.c b/drivers/gpu/drm/msm/adreno/adreno_device.c
index 7f20320ef..fb4320b56 100644
--- a/drivers/gpu/drm/msm/adreno/adreno_device.c
+++ b/drivers/gpu/drm/msm/adreno/adreno_device.c
@@ -120,6 +120,17 @@ struct msm_gpu *adreno_load_gpu(struct drm_device *dev)
 		goto err_put_rpm;
 	}
 
+	/*
+	 * Runtime power collapse leaves the A540 interconnect wedged on MSM8998.
+	 * Hold a device-managed reference until the collapse sequence is fixed.
+	 * System sleep still reaches the runtime callbacks through force suspend.
+	 */
+	if (adreno_is_a540(adreno_gpu)) {
+		ret = devm_pm_runtime_get_noresume(&pdev->dev);
+		if (ret)
+			goto err_put_rpm;
+	}
+
 	pm_runtime_put_autosuspend(&pdev->dev);
 
 #ifdef CONFIG_DEBUG_FS
